<!--BlockML Documentation — update A02 page skeletons
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task.A02_UpdatePageSkeletons-->
<task:A02_UpdatePageSkeletons xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that updates A02 page skeletons
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A02 structuring task: PagePlan.scopes name the topic only. This task reads
    authorativeSources, selects the matching SSOT Blocks, and writes each page
    skeleton with a formulated purpose plus see links to those sources. An
    existing skeleton is overwritten; its content is never used as input. Body
    content stays for a03.
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          PagePlan carries only name and scopes. scopes is a topic list — what the page
          is about — not a purpose, title, or outline. Structuring must open the
          authoritative sources, choose the SSOT Blocks that cover those scopes, and
          write a formulated purpose from what those Blocks actually say.

          1. Read the plan
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a01_planning.data.BmlDocSetPlan. Walk every nested
          PagePlan under rootPageGroupPlan. Ignore PageGroupPlan entries.

          2. Open the authoritative sources before writing a page
          Resolve this task's authorativeSources TypeSelectors (scan type for each
          selector). Also read BmlDocSetPlan.authoritativeSources (the core Library and
          the Blocks it owns). For each candidate, inspect is, documentation, and
          references — do not guess from the FQN or from scopes alone.

          3. Bind sources to scopes
          For each PagePlan, select the source Blocks whose documented subject matches
          that page's scopes. Those selected Blocks are the page's authoritative
          sources. Every page must have at least one Requires source. If several
          sources match, Requires = primary SSOT for the scopes; SeeAlso = supporting
          background. Do not attach a source that does not serve the scopes.

          4. Formulate the skeleton from the bound sources
          Resolve the A02 FQN as
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page + "." + PagePlan.name
          (for example docs.FirstBlock →
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.FirstBlock).
          Do not write under DocSetPlan.pageBasePackage (a03). Do not create or edit
          a03 pages, PageGroups, DocSet, or pageMapping.

          If a skeleton with that name already exists, discard its current content
          and regenerate the file from the plan and the bound authoritative sources.
          Existing skeleton content is never authoritative: do not treat it as true,
          and do not use it as input for generation (not is, documentation, purpose,
          title, see links, or any other field). Keep only the FQN / file path so
          the same Block is overwritten. Do not invent pages that are not in the plan.

          Write purpose as a finished renderer instruction: why this page exists and
          what it must accomplish, grounded in the bound sources (their is /
          documentation / claims). Do not copy scopes into purpose and do not leave
          purpose as a topic list.

          Each skeleton must:
          - use baseType org.blockml.bml.docgen.page.DocPage
            (not org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.Page)
          - set is to one short identity sentence informed by the bound sources
          - set documentation to name the scopes, name the bound source FQNs, and
            state that body content is authored in a03 from those sources
          - override title, purpose, detailLevel (org.blockml.bml.docgen.level.*),
            and pageType (org.blockml.bml.docgen.pagetype.*) from the bound sources
          - list each bound source as references/see (Requires or SeeAlso)
          - omit every aggregation, including DocPage.content and Page.rules /
            authoritativeSources / audiences / semantic lists. Do not author
            sections, paragraphs, or other page body
          - omit docset

          Export each A02 skeleton from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not
          already in the catalog. Do not remove a03 catalog entries.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <authorativeSources type="type:TypeSelectorEntity[]">
      <composition>
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.docgen.annotation.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.docgen.capability.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.constraint.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.core.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.definition.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.documentation.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.exception.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.group.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.language.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.mapping.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.meta.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.relation.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.service.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.status.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.type.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.unit.**" />
        <type:TypeSelectorEntity value="org.blockml.bml.validation.**" />
      </composition>
    </authorativeSources>
  </aggregations>
</task:A02_UpdatePageSkeletons>